5. TRAILER PROTOTYPES  (development and review; not part of the game export)
================================================================================
trailers/ contains five rendered review videos and their editable compositions. In
addition to Remotion and React (section 3), the render-time tools include Revideo
0.11.0 (MIT), Motion Canvas 3.17.2 (MIT), HyperFrames 0.8.214 (Apache-2.0),
GSAP 3.15.0 (GreenSock standard licence: https://gsap.com/standard-license), p5.js
1.11.10 (LGPL-2.1), Puppeteer (Apache-2.0), Chromium, Vite (MIT), and FFmpeg. The
bundled FFmpeg used by these Linux render scripts is configured with GPL components.
The tools and their dependency licences are installed separately with npm; they are
not embedded in the MP4 output or shipped with the game. Review applicable terms
before redistributing tools or publishing the trailers.

The screening room and trailer sources include copies of Courier Prime (Copyright 2015
The Courier Prime Project Authors), Oswald (Copyright 2016 The Oswald Project Authors),
and Patrick Hand (Copyright 2010–2012 Patrick Wagesreiter), all under SIL OFL 1.1.
The full copyright and licence texts are in trailers/media/fonts/*-OFL.txt.
The trailer city illustration is AI-generated concept art; visual-prototype material
and gameplay captures are identified in trailers/README.md and in the videos.

